From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: M5Stack Agent <agent@m5stack.local>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:25:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hw/gpio: let board bias win over temporary internal pulls

M5GFX identifies Cardputer ADV by temporarily enabling internal pull-downs
on G8/G9 and observing the board's external pull-ups. Treating the opposing
weak sources as an unknown conflict misidentified the board as the legacy
Cardputer, which then selected the wrong keyboard and display configuration.

Active and open-drain drive still wins before weak bias resolution, so an
I2C ACK/data zero remains able to pull either line low.
---
 hw/gpio/esp32_gpio.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/gpio/esp32_gpio.c b/hw/gpio/esp32_gpio.c
--- a/hw/gpio/esp32_gpio.c
+++ b/hw/gpio/esp32_gpio.c
@@ -227,13 +227,22 @@ static void gpio_snapshot_internal(Esp32GpioState *s, unsigned pin,
             out->level = out->external_level;
             out->source_mask = ESP32_GPIO_PAD_SOURCE_EXTERNAL;
         } else {
+            bool board_up = out->bias_up_count != 0;
+            bool board_down = out->bias_down_count != 0;
             bool up = out->bias_up_count || out->fun_pu;
             bool down = out->bias_down_count || out->fun_pd;
             if (out->bias_up_count) { out->source_mask |= ESP32_GPIO_PAD_SOURCE_BOARD_UP; }
             if (out->bias_down_count) { out->source_mask |= ESP32_GPIO_PAD_SOURCE_BOARD_DOWN; }
             if (out->fun_pu) { out->source_mask |= ESP32_GPIO_PAD_SOURCE_IOMUX_UP; }
             if (out->fun_pd) { out->source_mask |= ESP32_GPIO_PAD_SOURCE_IOMUX_DOWN; }
-            if (!out->pull_config_known) {
+            if (board_up != board_down) {
+                /* A board resistor is external to the SoC and is stronger
+                 * than the short-lived internal pull used by board probes.
+                 * Active/open-drain drive was handled above, so this cannot
+                 * prevent an I2C ACK/data zero from winning. */
+                out->known = true;
+                out->level = board_up;
+            } else if (!out->pull_config_known) {
                 out->blocker_mask |= ESP32_GPIO_PAD_BLOCK_RESET_UNKNOWN;
             } else if (up && down) {
                 out->conflict = true;
             } else if (up || down) {
